# Contributing

Thanks for helping improve namesearch. The project is pre-1.0 and has no
published release artifacts yet.

## Before opening a change

Read [README], [SUPPORT], and [SECURITY]. Keep changes focused on the
standalone namesearch repository; do not add Stowcloud service, transport, ACL,
or application behavior here.

For public API changes, explain compatibility impact and update release notes.
For SCNB changes, preserve existing v1 bytes and add an explicit format version
and migration/rollback plan before implementation. The index is disposable
cache state; source data remains authoritative.

## Local checks

Use Go 1.27.1 and run:

```sh
go test ./...
go vet ./...
go test -race ./...
```

Run `gofmt` on changed Go files. CI also checks Linux amd64/arm64 behavior and
non-Linux compilation. Keep tests deterministic and avoid relying on local
filesystem layout, network services, or private data.

## Pull requests

Describe the behavior change, tests run, dependency changes, format impact,
and rollback procedure. Do not commit generated binaries, local indexes, or
credentials. A maintainer listed in [MAINTAINERS] reviews all changes.

## Commit and release conventions

Use Conventional Commit subjects (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `ci:`,
`chore:`, and similar). Releases are maintainer decisions; until publication,
there is no promise of stable module versions. Every release note must state
whether SCNB bytes, public APIs, dependencies, or rollback behavior changed.

